From ee3fefa07c11ab19d9e01c1922108482acbf5505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:12:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(sim): a carried clip keeps NaN, stays empty once
 empty, refuses bad corners

Review of #651, three blockers:
- box_signed / distance: f64::max dropped a NaN, so a NaN point read -inf
  (deep inside) once clipped. NaN now stays NaN; inside() is false.
- then(): two clips that miss gave an inverted box that then() re-sorted
  into a real one - material reappeared after a turn. The clip is now an
  enum (Block | Empty) and Empty stays Empty through every turn.
- clipped(): a non-finite or inverted corner is refused by name
  (ClipRefusal::NonFinite / Inverted) instead of silently dropping an
  axis.
inside()'s doc now says it reads the uncut parity and that step D reads
distance().

Pinned by field_carry::a_nan_point_stays_nan_through_the_clip,
two_clips_that_miss_stay_empty_through_a_turn and
a_non_finite_or_inverted_clip_is_refused_by_name.

